# Tooling use (verified for this machine)

## Git sync (agent, not human)

- At **new Agent chat / pick-up**, before coding: `git pull origin main` (on `main`; stash if needed).
- At **slice close-out**: commit + `git push origin main`.
- Never ask the human to pull, commit, or push.

## Supermemory — use by default (v5 hosted MCP, plugin 1.3.1+)

Install: local `~/.cursor/plugins/local/cursor-supermemory` (v5). Do **not** call legacy tool names `supermemory_search` / `supermemory_add` / `workspaceRoot` / `container`.

- **Canonical project namespace:** `repo_ai_testing_app__bbdc87968dd0838c` (pass as `namespace` on every call; `containerTag` is a deprecated alias only).
- **Session start / pick-up:** `search_memory` with the user goal + “KAN Active slice” / architecture. Pass `namespace` above. Reuse `conversation_id` from the first Supermemory response for later calls in the same chat.
- **After decisions / slices:** `add_memory` with `content` + the same `namespace` (project facts). Prefer `list_spaces` if unsure which space key to use.
- **After hard bugs:** `add_memory` with root cause + fix (no secrets).
- Do **not** block the slice if a Supermemory MCP call fails; retry once, then continue with WORK_LOG / PROJECT_MEMORY.
- Never store secrets, tokens, or full settings.json in Supermemory.
- Never call `set-active-tag` / `select-space` to a different space unless the human asks — keep this repo on the canonical namespace.

## Jira

- Try user-atlassian; on API-token / permission errors → REST + local settings / `scripts/jira_kan_*.py` immediately.
- After slices: **required** close-out via `scripts/jira_kan_slice_closeout.py` (or equivalent REST) —
  story comment stating what the agent implemented, plus linked test Task evidence + Done.

## GitHub

- Use **plugin-github-github** for PRs/issues/repo. Do not enable workspace npx GitHub MCP.

## UI verification (desktop app first)

- **Primary product UI** is the **native desktop window**: `.\venv\Scripts\python.exe desktop_app.py` (pywebview + Edge WebView2). Run and verify it **as an application**, not by opening the shell URL in Chrome/Edge/IronBee.
- Do **not** treat `http://127.0.0.1:…/ui/desktop/` in a browser tab as the product.
- **Gradio** (`run_ui.py` / port 7860) only when the slice explicitly targets Gradio. Then IronBee browser is OK for Gradio only.
- **IronBee browser:** for the *application under test* (Playwright AUT pages) or Gradio-only checks — never as the default way to “open our app”. IronBee Node/Backend stay off unless asked.
- OS dialogs / Ollama Settings: Computer Use OK.

### Tiered Computer Use (GPU + overlay safety — Council 2026-11-18)

- **pytest / API / HTML first** for non-visual AC. Do not burn GPU on CU loops when markers + API already prove the story.
- **CU only** for visual / occlusion / clickable chrome (and OS UI). Throttle screenshots; short sessions.
- **Pre-CU quiet window:** pause Ollama for agent CU verify; prefer classic orb (avoid mystic/aether/neural WebGL + CU + Ollama together on the 1080 Ti). Human demos that need chat+UI together are exempt.
- **One overlay:** dismiss product Manual/Charter Frame before CU when the slice is not about that overlay. Cursor CU HUD vs product overlay → contested clicks / polluted shots (common in WORK_LOG).
- **When CU is unsafe:** one quiet retry, then document **CU skipped — unsafe** or **CU flake** on the test ticket. Never soft-pass on “opened orb home.” Occlusion stories still need clickable proof when a quiet desktop is achievable.
- **Human-hands handoff:** if the human must confirm (CU cannot), the agent prepares everything first: app running (or one start command), seeded data / stubs / fixtures ready, and a numbered step list in chat + test ticket (clicks, inputs, expected pass). Human only follows and confirms — no setup hunting. Do not mark occlusion/visual AC Done until human confirm (or CU) lands.
- Build-time agent GPU load ≠ product-runtime GPU budget — do not invent product FRs or in-app verify chrome to fix Cursor CU.

## Context7 / library docs (stale-advice gate)

This project rule **narrows** the plugin’s “when unsure” into a hard trigger. It does **not** weaken it into a skip. Token thrift does not override this gate.

- **Source order:** (1) repo code / security rules, (2) installed `venv` package, (3) Context7 or official docs for that version, (4) training memory last (label unverified).
- **Required before inventing/changing calls** to FastAPI, Pydantic, Playwright, Gradio, pywebview, Ollama HTTP API, or httpx (and auth/CORS/profile/credential surfaces). One resolve + one query per library per slice.
- **Skip** builtins, in-repo APIs, and copy of an already-working same-surface call.
- **Playwright:** match `async_api` in `plugins/playwright_runner.py`; do not add `sync_api` there.
- **On MCP error:** `pip show` / read installed package / official docs — continue; do not invent “latest.” Ignore Local Error·terminated if Cloud works.
- **Queries:** library + API only — no secrets, settings, tokens, or AUT data.
- Skill pointer: `.cursor/skills/context7-use/SKILL.md`. Product runtime never calls Context7.
